+// Exact projections of the remaining difference system after releasing all
+// and only constraints belonging to the specified routes. Every other path,
+// its shared tile identities, and every global anchor stay fixed. Each
+// interval is individually tight; choosing values from several intervals
+// independently does NOT establish joint realizability. Nor does it prove
+// that a new physical path exists: final geometry and global clock solving
+// are mandatory after route replacement. In particular, moving endpoints or
+// changing supposedly frozen paths invalidates this conditional contract.
+inline CombinationalClockWindowFeedback solveCombinationalClockArrivalWindows(
+    const CombinationalClockFeedback &feedback,
+    const std::vector<std::size_t> &releasedRoutes,
+    const std::vector<CombinationalClockWindowQuery> &queries,
+    const std::function<bool()> &cancelled = {})
